@page "/docs/components/image"
@using Blaizio.Docs.Examples.Image
<PageTitle>Image - Blaizio</PageTitle>

<div class="typeset typeset-docs space-y-10">
    <header class="docs-page-header space-y-2.5">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Image</h1>
            <DocBadges Slug="image" />
        </div>
        <p>A content image that tracks its own load state, so you can show a placeholder while it loads and a fallback with a retry button if it fails. A reserved aspect ratio keeps the layout from shifting, and the image fades in with CSS alone once it arrives. Everything runs off the browser's native <code>img</code> events with no polling, and <code>&lt;picture&gt;</code> sources cover responsive art direction.</p>
    </header>

    <UsageBlock Example="typeof(ImageDefaultExample)"
                Description="Set `Src`, `Alt` and an optional `Ratio` on the root. Add `BzImagePlaceholder`, `BzImageFallback` or `BzImageSource` children only when you need them." />

    <CompositionTree Root="Anatomy"
                     Description="Every part of an image. When `BzImageSource` children are present, the `img` renders inside a `picture`. The placeholder covers the box until the image loads or fails, and the fallback appears only on error." />

    <ExamplesHeading />

    <Demo Title="Default" Description="`Ratio` reserves the box before the image arrives, so nothing shifts, and the image fades in once it loads. Throttle your connection to watch it happen."
          Example="typeof(ImageDefaultExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Skeleton placeholder" Description="`BzImagePlaceholder` covers the image box until the image loads or fails. Put a `BzSkeleton` or any other loading treatment inside it, and it is removed once the image loads."
          Example="typeof(ImagePlaceholderExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Blur-up (LQIP)" Description="`PlaceholderSrc` paints a tiny blurred version under the real image and fades it out on load. In production, inline it as a data URI so the placeholder costs no extra request."
          Example="typeof(ImageBlurUpExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Error fallback" Description="`BzImageFallback` renders only when the source fails to load, so it can hold an icon, a hint or a stand-in graphic."
          Example="typeof(ImageFallbackExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Retry" Description="`Retry()` replaces the `img` element so the browser makes a fresh request. Keep a reference to the component and call it from a button inside the fallback."
          Example="typeof(ImageRetryExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Fit" Description="`Fit` maps to CSS `object-fit`. `Cover` crops the image to fill the box and `Contain` letterboxes it inside, while `Fill`, `None` and `ScaleDown` complete the set."
          Example="typeof(ImageFitExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Lazy loading" Description="Set `Loading` to `Lazy` to defer each request until the image nears the viewport, using the browser's native lazy loading. For the hero image that counts toward Largest Contentful Paint, set `FetchPriority` to `High` instead."
          Example="typeof(ImageLazyExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Responsive (picture)" Description="`BzImageSource` children wrap the `img` in a `picture` element. `Media` picks a source by viewport for art direction, `Type` picks one by format for AVIF or WebP fallback chains, and the image's own `Src` is the last resort."
          Example="typeof(ImageResponsiveExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Caption" Description="Setting `Caption` turns the root into a semantic `figure` and renders a styled `figcaption` under the image."
          Example="typeof(ImageCaptionExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Load status" Description="`StatusChanged` reports `Idle`, `Loading`, `Loaded` and `Error`, so you can drive anything the built-in slots don't cover."
          Example="typeof(ImageStatusExample)" />
</div>

@code {
    // The anatomy drawn by the Composition section - CompositionTree computes the connectors.
    private static readonly CompositionNode Anatomy = new("BzImage",
        new CompositionNode("BzImageSource"),
        new CompositionNode("BzImagePlaceholder"),
        new CompositionNode("BzImageFallback"));
}
